contentText:
With Forgotten Island &#8216;s central story of friendship and themes inspired by Philippines mythology, Filipino-American singer Sophia Laforteza of the global girl group KATSEYE was a fitting pick to make music for the DreamWorks Animation film.

In a new digital bonus feature debuting exclusively on Billboard , Sophia and her collaborators &#8212; including composer Nathan Matthew David, producer Mike Elizondo and writers/directors Joel Crawford and Januel P. Mercado &#8212; take viewers inside the studio to discuss the making of her cover of INXS&#8217; &#8220;Never Tear Us Apart&#8221; for the film, which arrives on digital platforms Tuesday (Oct. 27) with more than 60 minutes of bonus content.

