&#8220;‘Never Tear Us Apart’ is really kind of the journey of this movie and of the girls’ friendship – their anthem, in a way,&#8221; Crawford says of lead besties Raissa and Jo (voiced by singer/songwriter H.E.R.).

&#8220;For Sophia and Mike and Nathan to make it an interpretation that stands on its own is an incredible accomplishment,&#8221; Mercado adds of reinterpreting the 1988 top 10 Billboard Hot 100 hit for INXS.

For David, Sophia immediately impressed him in the studio. &#8220;Right from the beginning of her vocal session, we knew it was going to be really special. I think she just sang the hell out of this song.&#8221;

Sophia&#8217;s personal connection to the film as a Filipino American was what drove home the musical connection. &#8220;Hearing her talk about how she really has the story in her DNA, in her soul &#8212; what she brought to this, I can’t imagine anyone else,&#8221; Crawford says.

That story was Sophia&#8217;s north star as she navigated making &#8220;Never Tear Us Apart&#8221; her own. &#8220;As a performer, my strength is, if you tell me what the story is, I’ll tell it the best way that I can,&#8221; she says in the bonus feature. &#8220;I got to watch the scene while singing it, and I really tried to take every ounce of knowledge I knew just growing up in this world. This is one of the most beautiful things I think I’ll ever do.&#8221;

